---
project: emospace
---

## The context

We are in a time when online and offline retail are merging and customer-experience demands are changing. There is a "local products" movement, yet the traditional store owner is feeling left out — without effective, simple retail analytics.

## Design brief

How can we empower traditional shop owners with a service that helps them understand their customers better?

## How EmoSpace works

The system uses in-store security cameras together with context information — weather, events, shopping patterns, listed and learned competitors, and online prices — to build an information base. It runs on commercially available cloud AI platforms like Microsoft Azure. The data is analysed for patterns and, using a unique three-level information architecture, surfaced to the shopkeeper unobtrusively.

## A privacy-first approach

EmoSpace stores no personal data and cannot be used to identify customers. It performs simple recognition on the CCTV stream — signs of gender, age, and emotion — and images are discarded after processing automatically. The system is designed to follow GDPR and other privacy regulations.

## Daily store stories

Instead of bombarding the shopkeeper with numbers, EmoSpace adopts a data-sanity approach: a brief daily summary that can be consumed on the commute home or just before sleep. Each story has three levels of depth — summary, review, and charts.

## Impact

The shopkeeper becomes part of the data narrative around the store. They can act on confusion, space orientation, lighting, product placement, and even pricing — with real-time access as well as trends over six months, so they can see the impact of this low-cost service on their business.
